# Findus V5 — Booking Deep-Research Flow (Master Template)

## Pipeline (mandatory)

```
Deep-Search (live API/HTTP)
  → Parse inventory (times / prices / seats / tariffs)
  → Conversational upsell (time choice → baggage → exact total)
  → Action buttons = deep links scoped to the researched slots
```

Never invent “ca. 50–60 €”, “je nach Tide/Wetter” when a live source exists.

---

## Inselflieger — what works 1:1

| Step | Source | Status |
|------|--------|--------|
| Date + direction | Speech parse | ✅ |
| Live times/prices/seats | `GET https://www.inselflieger.de/api/flights?date=YYYY-MM-DD` | ✅ |
| Sold-out narrative | Compare `availability=sold` vs free slots | ✅ |
| Tariff explanation | Basic/Flex/Plus + kg allowances + Übergepäck 1,20 €/kg | ✅ |
| Time follow-up | Pending session + nearest free slots | ✅ |
| Deep link date/route | Frisonaut `assistent?destination=…&start=…` from API | ✅ |

### What does NOT work 1:1 (honest)

| Wish | Gap | Why | How to make it possible |
|------|-----|-----|-------------------------|
| Prefill First/Last/Email/Gender into Frisonaut checkout | Portal ignores extra query params | No public passenger deep-link API; SPA checkout | Partner deal with Frisia/Frisonaut for `guest=` tokens, OR in-app WebView with injected form fill (fragile), OR official booking API |
| Gender in URL | Not in `UserProfile` | Field never collected | Add optional `gender` in settings IF partner supports it |
| One-tap payment done | Impossible without their checkout API | Payment stays on Frisonaut | Deep link is best available |

Code: `src/services/flights/inselfliegerAdvisor.ts`

